 "result_text": "I fixed both problems in `pythonfmu/fmi2slave.py`, but I haven't run it or built an FMU to check. I also haven't validated the output with `fmpy`.\n\n- **Float error:** the `startTime`, `stopTime` and `tolerance` values are now converted with `str()` before they go into the XML. You can pass plain floats to `DefaultExperiment` without the `str(0.)` workaround.\n- **`fmpy` validation error:** `DefaultExperiment` was being written at the end of the model description, after `ModelStructure`. The FMI 2 schema wants it before `ModelVariables`, so the validator rejected it. I moved it to sit right after `LogCategories`, which is the schema order. So the validation error was a bug on the PythonFMU side, not in `fmpy`.",
